  "security_implications": "The chunk computes the message length used for HMAC SHA-2 padding. If digest_size_i is corrupted in inner pad mode, sha_msg_len defaults to 0, leading to incorrect HMAC length and potentially predictable authentication failures or bypass. The handling of SHA-512 in final hash mode falls through to the same value as SHA-384; if that mapping is wrong, HMAC tags will be broken. Both cases threaten integrity and authentication integrity.",
